<title>UK: EU to raise high quality wheat,maize import duties.</title>
<headline>EU to raise high quality wheat,maize import duties.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union will on Saturday increase duties on transatlantic imports of high-quality soft wheat and maize, European Commission figures showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>The import duty on high quality wheat will rise to 7.88 Ecus per tonne from 7.84 Ecus, while that for maize will be increased to 77.45 Ecus/tonne from a previous 76.80 Ecus.  </p>
<p>At the same time import duties on medium and low quality soft wheat will be lowered to 29.06 Ecus/tonne and 41.43 Ecus from 30.71 Ecus and 43.91 Ecus respectively.</p>
<p>Barley and rye import duties will be cut to 62.06 Ecus/tonne from 62.39 Ecus. Duties on sorghum imports will fall to 74.00 Ecus/tonne from 74.33 Ecus. Duty on durum wheat will remain unchanged at zero Ecus/tonne.</p>
</text>
